WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.990
A single nerve cell can receive
thousands of messages at once,

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.120
from many other nerve cells.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:11.150
Yet its own output is all or nothing:
it fires a full action potential,

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.510
or none at all.

5
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.430
Thousands of messages in.

6
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.970
One yes-or-no answer out.

7
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.390
So how does a nerve cell
decide whether to fire?

8
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.480
In this mission, you'll
zoom into the cell body,

9
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.770
where synapses from many other
cells crowd onto one membrane.

10
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.470
Then you'll track the
voltage of that membrane,

11
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.370
millisecond by millisecond,
against a threshold line.

12
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.270
Your mission: find out how one nerve cell,

13
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.400
receiving thousands of messages
at once, decides whether to fire.
